        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-16T03:00:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Given that mMapFd is not final: does it need to be marked volatile for this to be correct? finalizers can be invoked on any thread and so are not guaranteed to see the constructor\u0027s write to mMapFd.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 251,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 251,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "c29e1e24aaf9aef87b5b218a6aa4eac77152d2e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0678bcef_f7b71b72",
        "filename": "Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/BpfMap.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 251,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042828
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-17T00:34:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Assuming that a reachabilityFence(this) is executed as the last operation on the object, and all explicit calls to it are from a single thread, the finalizer shouldn\u0027t run concurrently with other accesses, and this should be OK.",
      "parentUuid": "be8f4d04_8a2be8a7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 251,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 251,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "c29e1e24aaf9aef87b5b218a6aa4eac77152d2e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "87be2092_aabf1353",
        "filename": "Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/BpfMap.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 253,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042828
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-17T00:34:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That needs to go at the end of the finally clause, to make sure the finalizer can\u0027t run before mGuard.close() executes. This is the one reachabilityFence that you really need to keep if you don\u0027t use @ReachabilitySensitive.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 253,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 253,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "c29e1e24aaf9aef87b5b218a6aa4eac77152d2e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d85bb083_7eec4c70",
        "filename": "Tethering/src/com/android/networkstack/tethering/BpfMap.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 261,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-02-16T03:00:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this can this actually happen, given that the write to mGuard happens before an exception can be thrown. When the exception is thrown, the constructor terminates abruptly, and a freeze happens on mGuard.\n\nhttps://docs.oracle.com/javase/specs/jls/se8/html/jls-17.html#jls-17.5.1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 261,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 261,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "c29e1e24aaf9aef87b5b218a6aa4eac77152d2e8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
