      "writtenOn": "2021-02-17T00:34:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Interesting question.\n\nPresumably if the CloseGuard allocation fails, we end up with a null mGuard. I think the finalizer should not run in this case, but I\u0027m not immediately certain, since we have a bug dealing with registering finalizers too early. See b/63177201. I would replace the comment with something like:\n\n// We defensively assume mGuard might be null. See b/63177201.\n\n... and leave the code as is.",
